    "content": "In July 2025, it was announced that Donald Trump was diagnosed with chronic venous insufficiency (CVI), a common, generally benign, but sometimes uncomfortable vascular condition where leg veins struggle to return blood to the heart, causing swelling. It is not a direct heart disease, but a condition affecting circulation, often related to age. Key Details of the Diagnosis: Cause: The condition involves a malfunction in the vein valves, leading to blood pooling in the lower legs and causing swelling. Symptoms & Presentation: Trump experienced mild leg swelling and some skin discoloration/bruising. Heart Health: Physicians found no evidence of deep vein thrombosis (DVT), heart failure, or heart structural issues during the evaluation. Management: CVI is common in older adults (10–30% prevalence) and is typically managed rather than cured. While the White House reported that the President remains in \"excellent health,\" he also maintains a standard cardiovascular prevention regimen, which includes the use of aspirin.",
